    "Inflammation promotes atherosclerosis, affecting chronic rheumatologic inflammatory joint disorders such as systemic lupus erythematosus, rheumatoid arthritis (RA), and psoriasis, increasing cardiovascular disease (CVD) risks. Individuals with HIV or hepatitis C virus co-infection have elevated ASCVD risks. RA patients have increased lipid levels, which are exacerbated by some anti-inflammatory treatments. Accurate ASCVD risk assessment in these conditions is vital, emphasizing lifestyle and risk factor management.": [],
